cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LensForge, its rendered images, or its validation methodology in
  academic work, please cite it as below.
title: "LensForge: a physically rigorous real-time Kerr black-hole renderer for the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The LensForge Authors"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-19"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - black hole
  - Kerr metric
  - general relativity
  - gravitational lensing
  - relativistic ray tracing
  - Novikov-Thorne disk
  - WebGPU
  - scientific visualization
abstract: >-
  LensForge renders a Kerr black hole by numerically integrating null
  geodesics (Hamiltonian formulation, adaptive Dormand-Prince 4(5)) in WebGPU
  compute shaders, with exact relativistic radiometry for a Novikov-Thorne
  thin accretion disk and a real star catalog under computed lensing
  magnification. A float64 CPU oracle implementing identical physics is
  validated against closed-form general relativity on every commit, and the
  float32 GPU implementation is validated against the oracle and against
  published results (Bardeen shadow contour, Luminet 1979 disk geometry,
  DNGR beaming morphology). Measured accuracy bounds ship with the release.
